  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 PM EST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nBroad surface high pressure remains over the region and mid/upper\nlevel ridging continues to build in from the west. We will see \ndry weather through the remainder of the work week, and the \nwarming trend will continue with high temperatures by Friday \nexpected to be around 5 to 10 degrees above normal. Afternoon \nrelative humidity values will be quite low through at least \nThursday, although winds will be on the light side which will help\nto mitigate fire weather concerns. \n\nBy the weekend, models are generally converging on a scenario where \none upper wave/weak low pressure system tracks by to our southeast \nSaturday then another short wave and weak cold front approaches from \nthe west before moving across our area around the Sunday/Sunday \nnight time frame.  Models are showing poor agreement/consistency \nwith these features, but overall there is general agreement that \nmoisture will be limited.  Right now, the NBM is showing some low \nchances for light precipitation this weekend, and this looks \nreasonable for now. \n\nMonday and Tuesday look dry behind the front, with temperatures \nback down closer to seasonal normals. &&",
